    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0288" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg30"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/60a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-26T21:51:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 26, 1915, 9.51 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1472. Department informed by Associated Press steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Noordam</hi>, carrying American delegates to International Peace Congress
                    at The Hague, anchored in the Downs unable to obtain permission to proceed up
                    the channel to Rotterdam.</p>
                <p>If report is true, please communicate with Foreign Office immediately and inquire
                    whether arrangements cannot be made in order that American delegates may reach
                    their destination in time for conference April 28.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
